  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Acciones de base comunitaria para el desarrollo sostenible y conservacin en Darin, Panam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the face of widespread loss of the Darien Rainforest, the Embera and Wounaan Indigenous communities in Panama have shifted from hunter gathering to farming. These communities need to ensure their food security, yet may put their long-term livelihoods at risk if they use agricultural techniques that further damage the fragile forest ecosystem. The IAF supports community-led approaches to strengthen resilience through sustainable agriculture. Our grantee partner, Fundacin Rapaces y Bosques - Panam (FRBP), supports Indigenous communities in the Darien to adopt sustainable agricultural practices that increase incomes and food security while also protecting rainforest ecosystems.This grant is part of the IAF&apos;s broader COVID-19 response strategy.</narrative>
  </description>
